        raise AssertionError("Will never reach here")
```

The issue is related to splitting cells. The problem statement mentions an issue in `textual`.
If `cell_pos > cut`, it currently does:
```python
                return (
                    _Segment(before[: pos - 1] + " ", style, control),
                    _Segment(" " + text[pos:], style, control),
                )
```
This looks like it's trying to handle cases where a character spans multiple cells (like an emoji) and the cut falls in the middle of it. It replaces the character with two spaces.

Wait, if `cell_pos > cut`, it means the character at `text[pos-1]` (since `pos` was incremented) made `cell_pos` exceed `cut`.
`before` is `text[:pos]`.
`before[: pos - 1]` is `text[:pos-1]`.
So it's replacing the character at `text[pos-1]` with a space in both segments.

