steps.message:
The bug in `Segment._split_cells` was that it would split a segment immediately when the `cell_pos` reached the `cut` position, potentially separating zero-width characters (like combining marks) from the characters they modify.

I updated the `_split_cells` method to continue consuming characters as long as they have a cell size of 0 after the `cut` position has been reached. This ensures that all trailing zero-width characters are included in the first segment, preserving the integrity of the text.

```python
            if cell_pos == cut:
                while pos < len(text) and cell_size(text[pos]) == 0:
                    pos += 1
                return (
                    _Segment(text[:pos], style, control),
                    _Segment(text[pos:], style, control),
                )
```

This fix preserves the total cell length of the segments while correctly handling zero-width characters. Existing tests were verified to still pass.
